# Allowlist, not a denylist. The build context is the repo root for all three
# images (Dockerfile, Dockerfile.kerberos, loadgen/Dockerfile) and the daemon
# receives the entire context regardless of which paths the Dockerfile COPYs.
# Before this file, every build shipped ~12 GB and took ~10 minutes just to
# transfer — target/ is 76 GB and .claude/ and .superpowers/ are tens more.
#
# A denylist would need updating every time a new large directory appears at
# the root, and would silently regress when someone forgets. This inverts it:
# nothing is sent unless named here. All three Dockerfiles COPY exactly the
# same five paths — keep this in sync if that changes, or the build fails
# loudly at COPY (not silently).
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!src
!tools
!benches
!logthing.toml
